// A module importing, with 'use *', a module that EXTENDS it: a loop, one edge
// an import and the other an 'extends'. Imports form a DAG [Jon 23 Sep], and
// 'extends' is a dependency like an import, so each pair is refused
// (ErrorImportLoop) at the edge that closes it.
//
// It is here twice, in both orders, because which edge closes the loop is what
// decides where it is reported: the walk that orders the modules starts from the
// one the program holds first. Importer first, the extender's 'extends' closes
// it; extender first, the importer's import does. Either way it is one
// diagnostic, and the loop is not cut: the fold passes still carry each module's
// names round it, so nothing the loop left half-folded is reported missing.
//
// The folder holds:
//   base/base.cone     imports rich with 'use *'; held before rich
//   rich/rich.cone     extends base
//   alpha/alpha.cone   extends omega; held before omega
//   omega/omega.cone   imports alpha with 'use *'

fn reach() i64 {
  base.useRich() + omega.useAlpha();
}
